// dsl/extdeps/diagnostic/mock_corpus.dag
// Scope: the diagnostic layer's PUBLISHED mock corpus as a closed, declared structural fact.
// Anchor: DESIGN.md §3 (single authority) / §6 (model-just-in-time, mark the carrier).
//
// SINGLE authority for WHICH diagnostic.* / redfish.Http operations are hermetically realizable.
// Read by BOTH the compile-time M2 mock_totality_lens (src/v2/lens/mock_totality.dag, via the
// per-layer witness) AND the v1 runtime's eval_service_call (the M4 hermetic-realization fold) —
// one model, not two. The v1 runtime loads the dsl/ tree, so this corpus lives in dsl/ for the
// runtime to reach the SAME model the lens reads. Modeled on the M4.0 filesystem pilot
// (dsl/extdeps/filesystem/mock_corpus.dag, #5188).
//
// Per-SERVICE governance: eval_service_call splits an operation_key on its last `.`, so each of
// diagnostic.ssh.Session / redfish.Http / diagnostic.edac.RasMcCtl / diagnostic.ipmi.Tool is
// governed independently. Every op that today carries an inline mock_response IS published below,
// so no governed service's sibling is silently fail-closed.
//
// Rows inhabit std.hermetic_replay.PublishedMockCase. The operation set authority remains the
// service decls under dsl/extdeps/diagnostic/{ssh,edac,ipmi}.dag and
// dsl/extdeps/bmc/http.dag (redfish.Http); per-case payloads live in the Phase-2
// RecordedFixture store ONLY — rows carry the structural key (service, operation,
// operation_key, case_id).

module extdeps.diagnostic.mock_corpus

import std.hermetic_replay { PublishedMockCase }

data diagnostic_ssh_session_mock_case_exec: PublishedMockCase = PublishedMockCase {
  operation_key: "diagnostic.ssh.Session.Exec",
  service: "diagnostic.ssh.Session",
  operation: "Exec",
  case_id: 0
}

data diagnostic_ssh_session_mock_case_reachability: PublishedMockCase = PublishedMockCase {
  operation_key: "diagnostic.ssh.Session.Reachability",
  service: "diagnostic.ssh.Session",
  operation: "Reachability",
  case_id: 0
}

